{"title":"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A straight line passing through the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/559c5f1a789e7c0b85a47cea72d5217259ecb924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is perpendicular to the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8d717ffbac714f52f6a1b56b9df6b89a8a17bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-3y-7=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" />. Its equation is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/f/30f7135705443aeb670e78ae6b00264cd3847c07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } y+3x-4=0\\quad \\text{(B) } y+3x+4=0\\quad \\text{(C) } y-3x-4=0\\quad \\\\ \\text{(D) } 3y+x-12=0\\quad \\text{(E) } 3y-x-12=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"472\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The original line can be adjusted to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Standard_form\" title=\"Standard form\">standard form</a>, in which it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4c4409975272a5f3a40ff0fb6123f8a9874baed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-3y=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />. Because this line is in standard form, its slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4cecbd954413289e60fc7b89015c152e37ef0af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-1}{-3}=\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, the slope of the perpendicular line is the negative reciprocal of this number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b31b51deaa1a9e903d120a02141556c3e70e348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. Because we know that this new line passes through the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/9/559c5f1a789e7c0b85a47cea72d5217259ecb924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, we can describe this line using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point-slope_form\" title=\"Point-slope form\">point-slope form</a>, in which it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/072b414deee66a0f129bb25a4f7b31e52a1296a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y-4=-3(x-0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fbaddaed52d66c7eb9397bdc73eb42af41b383aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+3x-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" />, which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME\" title=\"1968 AHSME\">1968 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1968 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1968\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1968 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1968_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"